    "result_text": "I added `require_setting(key)` to `hc/front/decorators.py`. I haven't run the tests or the app.\n\nThe integrations views already import `require_setting` from that module and use it, for example `@require_setting(\"APPRISE_ENABLED\")`. The module had the imports but not the function, so those imports had nothing to load.\n\nThe decorator returns a 404 when `getattr(settings, key)` is falsy and calls the view normally otherwise. It comes from the catalog pattern `views.require_setting@v1`, with the `# pcat:` marker kept above it. `check_code` found no deviations from the pattern.\n\nThe decorator raises `AttributeError` if the setting isn't defined at all. This is how the catalog pattern behaves, and I left it as is."
